  "hypothesis": "Stance-ground round 3 (DECISIONS #171 tuning; owner-directed lever). Round 2 selected wane (striker edge in band at +0.467 pooled, mirrors healthy) but left bulwark-vs-fabricator at -0.467 against the 0.40 gate, with the shell exonerated by the diagnostic column (-0.067). The map's anchor-forbidden tag rations the stance system (112/233 open tiles; shell never on ground it holds; volley castable ~6% of standoff ticks). The free arm drops the tag kind from the VOLLEY and AEGIS SHELL entries only (turret anchors keep it; a held level split by tile set is a map-format question, deferred). Cells: strict/free on wane fabricator pairs, and on plain rig for bulwark-vs-striker (the in-band edge this lever also touches) and the bulwark mirror (shell-standoff pacing risk). The fabricator mirror carries no stance, cannot change bytes, and is not re-run. Gates: T1 controls replicate (bvf-strict within 0.25 of -0.467; fvs-strict within 0.25 of +0.467; bvs-strict within 0.25 of +0.600); T2 bvf-free reaches |payoff| <= 0.40; T2b fvs-free stays |payoff| <= 0.40; DN1 bvs-free stays |payoff| <= 0.40 and shifts no more than 0.30 from bvs-strict; DN2 bulwark-mirror-free draws and capped shares within +0.05 of strict. SELECTION: adopt berth (wane + free) as the tuned default iff T2, T2b, DN1, and DN2 all pass; otherwise adopt wane alone (round-2 selection) and return the stance-ground question to the owner with these numbers. Population and doctrine disclosures carry over; additionally the wave-4 bots were authored under strict placement, so free-arm stance usage on newly legal tiles is opportunistic rather than doctrinal -- measured adoption on those tiles is a lower bound.",
